# GuardBox reverse proxy
# Caddy terminates TLS and forwards to the API container.
# - tls internal + on_demand: Caddy issues its own CA cert on the fly for
#   whatever hostname/IP a client connects with (localhost, a LAN IP, a
#   self-hosted domain) — no public domain needed. Without "on_demand",
#   Caddy has no site address to bind an auto-issued cert to and refuses
#   every SNI with "no certificate available".
#   Install Caddy's root CA on client devices to avoid trust warnings:
#   https://caddyserver.com/docs/automatic-https#local-https
# - To use a public CA (Let's Encrypt) instead, replace ":443" with your
#   domain name and drop "tls internal { on_demand }".

:443 {
    tls internal {
        on_demand
    }
    reverse_proxy api:8000
}

:80 {
    redir https://{host}{uri} permanent
}
